  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Raffaele Costa began his finance career in Goldman Sachs Private Client Services before joining GLG Partners in its formative period. As a founding partner, he traded European and North American equities, co-managed a multi-strategy fund and helped shape products and client relationships. After GLG was acquired by Man Group, Costa led client advisory and product strategy across Europe and North America.\n\nFounding Tyndaris gave Costa an independent platform spanning hedge-fund strategies and property finance. Its real-estate arm arranged senior, mezzanine and preferred-equity capital for European transactions, building on his experience in alternative investments. He combined fund management with the design and distribution of specialised products for institutional and private clients. That progression from trader to founding partner and investment-company founder defines a career built around cross-border capital management.",
    "html": "<p>Raffaele Costa began his finance career in Goldman Sachs Private Client Services before joining GLG Partners in its formative period. As a founding partner, he traded European and North American equities, co-managed a multi-strategy fund and helped shape products and client relationships. After GLG was acquired by Man Group, Costa led client advisory and product strategy across Europe and North America.</p>\r\n<p>Founding Tyndaris gave Costa an independent platform spanning hedge-fund strategies and property finance. Its real-estate arm arranged senior, mezzanine and preferred-equity capital for European transactions, building on his experience in alternative investments. He combined fund management with the design and distribution of specialised products for institutional and private clients. That progression from trader to founding partner and investment-company founder defines a career built around cross-border capital management.</p>\r\n",
